%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 22d0308a90dc49ae97395f1b651723b5, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_COMM_01_CheaperIncumbent
  questionId: COMM-01
  category: 2
  speakerName: Sales Director
  questionText: >-
    Procurement says the incumbent is cheaper and good enough. The champion is nervous. What is your next move?
  answerOptions:
  - {fileID: 11400001}
  - {fileID: 11400002}
  - {fileID: 11400003}
  - {fileID: 11400004}
--- !u!114 &11400001
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_COMM_01_A1
  answerText: >-
    Discount early to protect momentum, then ask legal to accelerate paper.
  technicalDelta: -1
  commercialDelta: 0
  rapportDelta: -1
  energyDelta: -2
--- !u!114 &11400002
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_COMM_01_A2
  answerText: >-
    Rebuild the cost of inaction with the champion and arm them with a concise internal business case.
  technicalDelta: 0
  commercialDelta: 3
  rapportDelta: 2
  energyDelta: 0
--- !u!114 &11400003
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_COMM_01_A3
  answerText: >-
    Challenge procurement directly and explain that cheaper security usually means hidden risk.
  technicalDelta: 1
  commercialDelta: 1
  rapportDelta: -2
  energyDelta: -1
--- !u!114 &11400004
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 0d521c6b84db4b8fae30e3785d9e9582, type: 3}
  m_Name: Q_COMM_01_A4
  answerText: >-
    Ask what 'good enough' means operationally, then tie gaps to renewal risk, audit pressure, and incident response cost.
  technicalDelta: 1
  commercialDelta: 3
  rapportDelta: 1
  energyDelta: -1
